								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=308"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6797#msg6797"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=751.msg6797#msg6797">Re:Good guild going bad</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #24 on:</b> April 07, 2004, 08:33:26 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Derail....<br /><br />Regarding anon posting - you really need to figure out what you&#039;re going to do and stay consistent. &nbsp; Threatening to ban names, IP&#039;s, etc is totally opposite to what the rules <span style="text-decoration: underline;">you </span> created state<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Kinladar link=board=10;threadid=751;start=0#msg6761 date=1081279371</div><div class="quote">You can create a bogus name, that I&#039;ll ban the name the first time or two, then check for matching IP&#039;s and if need be ban IP ranges.</div><br />And the rules state:<br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">There is a Rants and Raves section that is completely unmoderated, and will stay as such. <span style="text-decoration: underline;">The only thing that may get someone banned would be if they continually flame using anon names</span>. We have no problem with someone flaming others in that section, and said flames will not be edited or, removed but the poster may find them selves banned for not having the guts to use a real EQ name. (*<span style="text-decoration: underline;">Granted, we will not spend undo time trying to find name spoofers, however, obvious anon names that are created with the sole purpose to flame others may be scrutinized</span>.)<br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
